Nested If-Else Statements in C

Today, I created a Ticket Price Discount program using the C programming language.

Through this program, I learned:

How to use the bool data type to store true or false values.
How to include the stdbool.h header file to work with Boolean values.
How to use if-else statements for decision-making.
How to use nested if-else statements (an if statement inside another if statement).
How to check multiple conditions, such as student and senior citizen discounts.
How to use compound assignment operators like *=.
How to calculate discounts using percentage values.
How to display prices with two decimal places using %.2f.
Important Logic / Formula

Discount Logic

Student + Senior: 30% discount (price *= 0.7)
Student only: 10% discount (price *= 0.9)
Senior only: 20% discount (price *= 0.8)
Neither: No discount (original price remains unchanged).

Important Variables

float price = 10.00; – Stores the original ticket price.
bool isStudent = false; – Checks whether the customer is a student.
bool isSenior = false; – Checks whether the customer is a senior citizen.
Project Goal

To understand and practice nested if-else statements and Boolean conditions in C. This program demonstrates how multiple conditions can be checked to apply different discounts to a ticket price. 
It also helped me understand Boolean values, conditional logic, percentage calculations, and formatted output.